        "comments": "The assembly llColAutu1.hap1.1 is based on 41x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The order and orientation of the scaffolds on Chromosome 3 68.17 Mbp - 70.32 Mbp, Chromosome 4 90.98 Mbp - 92.59 Mbp, Chromosome 28 11.67 Mbp - 12.35 Mbp and Chromosome 29 28.58 Mbp - 30.46 Mbp are uncertain. We can see two very faded HiC signal lines on the map for each pair of chromosomes, indicating that the species could have been tetraploid, but now it works as a functional diploid.",
